    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Energy, Texas was founded in 1896 by store owners Will and Charlie Baxter, who named it to honor the energetic spirit of its early residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/energy_texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened in Energy the same year it was founded and has stayed open through 2023, serving as a quiet reminder of the town’s long‑standing community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/energy_texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Energy sits on Farm Road 1702, about sixteen miles southeast of Comanche, a detail that places it firmly within the heart of Comanche County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/energy-tx",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The nearby Leon River, flowing roughly five miles south, has historically shaped local ranching and farming by providing essential water for livestock and crops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/energy_texas",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In its early days, Energy developed as a modest rural outpost that facilitated mail, news, and supplies for the first families settling in the area.",
